# What this repository is counted as.
#
# The product is the Go build. The Node implementation stays beside it as the previous
# product, the comparison baseline and the documented rollback path, so the tree is mostly
# JavaScript by file count -- and the language statistics then describe the repository as a
# JavaScript project, which is a statement about its past rather than about what it ships.
#
# detectable=false and nothing else. linguist-vendored would claim this code is somebody
# else's and linguist-generated would claim a machine wrote it. Both are false for src and
# poc, and the origin of verification/schema is not recorded anywhere here -- so it does not
# get a provenance claim either, only exclusion from the count.
#
# This adds no text or eol attribute, so line ending handling is exactly what it was.
src/**          linguist-detectable=false
poc/**          linguist-detectable=false
verification/** linguist-detectable=false
